codex
IRWB-028 is committed, with one limitation in F5: the corpus-wide exact byte totals were replaced by checks that each compiler produces a nonempty image. That allows new projects, but it no longer checks the original aggregate size property. The representative per-project byte assertions remain. No changes were pushed.

- **F2 — `f3ba438`, follow-up `4fecfc4`:** The new `f32-backend` regression failed with “Missing expected exception” when signatures were omitted. Signatures are now required, and callers supply them. Files: `src/typed/backend/run.ts`, `tools/reference-check.mjs`, `corpus/projects/chess-search/scripts/fixtures.mjs`, and the backend, f32-backend, bytecode-vm, regex-nfa and lz-roundtrip tests.
- **F3 — `8090e90`:** The new `reference-check` test requested `blend` but saw 83 functions instead of one. It now checks selection and unknown IDs. Files: `tools/reference-check.mjs`, `tests/typed/reference-check.test.mjs`.
- **F4 — `2b26ef9`:** The new format test showed continuation lines losing their indentation. It now checks indentation and idempotence. Files: `src/typed/format.ts`, `tests/typed/format.test.mjs`.
- **F5 — `6e83139`:** Changed `backend.test.mjs` to check agreement and case accounting, `passes.test.mjs` to check case accounting, `ssa.test.mjs` to check each function’s SSA results, and `tape.test.mjs` to check each project’s lift comparison. The changed tests passed on the current corpus and with a temporary valid project copy. The byte-total limitation above remains.
- **F6 — `f212153`:** The new corpus-wide workbench test first failed because `parseProjectMeta` did not exist. Both consumers now use it, and the test compares their metadata for every corpus project. Files: `src/typed/project.ts`, `src/workbench/projects.ts`, `tests/workbench/wb.test.mjs`.

The [ticket diary](/home/manuel/code/wesen/2026-11-24--compiler-workbench/.claude/worktrees/fix2-tl-irwb-028/ttmp/2026/11/26/IRWB-028--typed-side-fixes-f2-to-f6/reference/01-diary.md) records the failures and decisions. The build passed. The last requested Typed and workbench run reported **176 tests: 173 passed, 0 failed, 3 skipped**. Prettier was unavailable in the worktree, so the TypeScript formatting was maintained manually.
